      "css": ".ds-masthead { position: relative; overflow: hidden; color: var(--ink); background: var(--paper-sunk); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); } .ds-guilloche { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; fill: none; stroke: var(--guilloche); stroke-width: 0.5; opacity: 0.4; pointer-events: none; } .ds-masthead-row { position: relative; padding: var(--space-5) var(--space-4) var(--space-4); } .ds-wordmark { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.1; } .ds-masthead-note { display: inline-block; margin: 6px 0 0 -6px; padding: 1px 6px; font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 500; background: var(--paper-sunk); border-radius: 2px; }"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tool Bar",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "tool",
      "description": "Fixed bottom row of icon-over-label tools; the active tool fills with indigo.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-tools\"><button class=\"ds-tool\" aria-pressed=\"true\"><svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.75\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 20l1-4L16 5l3 3L8 19l-4 1Zm10-13 3 3\"/></svg> Dibujar</button><button class=\"ds-tool\" aria-pressed=\"false\"><svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.75\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 6V4h14v2M12 4v16m-3 0h6\"/></svg> Texto</button></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-tools { display: flex; justify-content: space-around; padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-1); background: var(--paper); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); } .ds-tool { flex: 1 1 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 2px; min-height: 56px; padding: var(--space-1); font: inherit; font-size: 0.8125rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); background: transparent; border: 0; border-radius: var(--radius); cursor: pointer; } .ds-tool:hover:not([aria-pressed='true']), .ds-tool:active:not([aria-pressed='true']) { background: var(--paper-sunk); } .ds-tool[aria-pressed='true'] { color: var(--on-primary); background: var(--primary); } .ds-tool:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--focus); outline-offset: 2px; }"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Document of Record",
    "overview": "A scanned page is a document of record, so the app dresses like security paper instead of a utility. The ground is pale lilac safety paper, the band at the top of every screen carries fine procedural guilloche line work, text and primary actions print in indigo ink, and each document is a numbered cheque stub with a perforated line between its image and its record.\n\nThe density is Operate mode: a one-handed tool used at a table in mixed indoor light. Controls are large and plain, surfaces are flat, and the identity lives in a few printed details rather than in decoration. Those details recede around the work: document images are the only saturated imagery, and the crop and camera screens hand almost everything over to the photo. Night mode is the same sheet printed in pale ink on deep indigo, following the system setting.\n\nThe system rejects the white list with a floating button and a saturated brand bar. It must also never resemble CamScanner in icon or visual design.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Pale lilac paper, indigo ink, carmine reserved for serials and danger.",
      "A guilloche band heads every paper screen; a rosette watermark appears only on the empty library.",
      "Cheque stubs with a dashed perforation and a typewritten serial.",
      "Flat surfaces separated by 1px rules, with a shadow only on sheets and floating layers.",
      "A fixed bottom action bar at thumb height.",
      "Motion is brief state feedback, plus one guilloche sweep before the camera opens."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Carmine Rule",
        "body": "Carmine prints only serial numbers and destructive or invalid states. Nothing else on the sheet may use it, so a red mark always means either \"this is the number\" or \"this is dangerous\".",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Saturated Document Rule",
        "body": "Document images are the only saturated imagery on a screen. Interface color stays in the lilac and indigo family, apart from carmine.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Night Printing Rule",
        "body": "Night mode changes the printing, not the design. Every role keeps its job and only its value changes, driven by the system color scheme with no in-app switch.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Three Faces Rule",
        "body": "Bodoni names, the system face operates, Courier Prime numbers. Courier Prime appears on serials and nowhere else; Bodoni never sets running text or a control label.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Plate Rule",
        "body": "Text smaller than a title never prints directly over line work. The masthead promise sits on a small plate of `paper-sunk` that interrupts the guilloche, as an overprint would.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Counted Numeral Rule",
        "body": "A page number set inside a Bodoni title uses the system face at 1.0625rem with tabular numerals, because a Bodoni 1 reads as a roman I. Page numbers elsewhere use tabular numerals in the body face.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Thumb Reach Rule",
        "body": "A screen's main action lives in the fixed bottom bar at thumb height. Where that bar holds tools instead, as in annotation, the commit action moves to the toolbar.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tap Floor Rule",
        "body": "Every touch target is at least 44px, including invisible hit areas on crop handles and annotation resize handles. Ordinary buttons are 48px, tools 56px, and the lead action 64px.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sheet Shadow Rule",
        "body": "Shadows belong to paper lying on the desk and to layers floating above the screen. Stubs, tiles, buttons, panels, notices and bars get a rule, not a shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Perforation Rule",
        "body": "A dashed line means paper that tears, an outline waiting to be filled, or a guide. It marks the 2px perforation on stubs and tiles, the border of the blank stub, the camera's card guide, and the 1px selection around an annotation. It is not general decoration for ordinary panels.",
        "section": "shapes"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Instrument Rule",
        "body": "Full circles are reserved for things that act like physical instruments: the camera shutter, crop and resize handles, and the magnifying lens. Interface buttons stay rectangular.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do head every paper screen with the guilloche band on `paper-sunk`, keeping line work at 40% opacity at rest.",
      "Do show documents as contained, unrounded images in a `paper-sunk` well with the Sheet shadow.",
      "Do put a 2px dashed perforation between a document's image and its record.",
      "Do use only the existing spacing scale (4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32px) and the 6px radius for new surfaces.",
      "Do define any new color for both the day and night printing, holding text at 4.5:1 or better.",
      "Do keep state motion within 150 to 250ms using `cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)`, and honor reduced motion.",
      "Do say plainly where documents live and what is not backed up, using the notice or the masthead promise."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't build the white list with a floating button and a saturated brand bar. Primary actions live in the bottom bar.",
      "Don't resemble CamScanner in icon or visual design.",
      "Don't use carmine for anything but serials and destructive or invalid states.",
      "Don't place line work or the rosette behind a document preview.",
      "Don't show the rosette anywhere but the empty library, or on viewports under 820px tall.",
      "Don't use Courier Prime for anything but serial numbers.",
      "Don't put small labels or uppercase tracked text above headings; the only tracked text in the system is the serial.",
      "Don't add a shadow to stubs, tiles, buttons, panels or bars.",
      "Don't apply the paper theme or the night printing to the camera; it stays dark in both.",
      "Don't add a second signature animation; the guilloche sweep before the camera is the only one."
    ]
  }
}
